//! [include_flags]
At least one of \a includeStatic and \a includeDynamic must be \c true. If both are
\c false the query does no work and reports no hit.
//! [include_flags]

//! [query_exclusions]
Trigger bodies, such as \l TriggerBody, are not colliders and are never reported. The
\l {PhysicsNode::filterGroup} {filterGroup} and
\l {PhysicsNode::filterIgnoreGroups} {filterIgnoreGroups} properties affect simulation
collisions only; scene queries ignore them.
//! [query_exclusions]

//! [hit_miss_return]
If nothing is hit, or the arguments are invalid, the returned hit has a \c null \c body.
Every body in the scene has an associated node, so \c {hit.body === null} is the reliable
test for a miss; the \c distance of a missed hit is \c 0 and carries no meaning.
//! [hit_miss_return]

//! [mesh_raycast_limits]
A ray that starts inside a mesh, or that exits through a back-facing triangle, does not
report that mesh.
//! [mesh_raycast_limits]

//! [mesh_multi_intersection]
Triangle mesh and heightfield shapes are reported once, at their closest intersection.
The individual triangles of one mesh are not returned as separate hits.
//! [mesh_multi_intersection]

//! [query_shape]
The \a shape supplies the geometry of the query as well as its starting position and
orientation: it is evaluated at its current scene transform, and any scaling on its node,
including scaling inherited from parent nodes, is baked into the query geometry. Only
\l BoxShape, \l SphereShape, \l CapsuleShape and \l ConvexMeshShape can be used; passing
\l PlaneShape, \l TriangleMeshShape or \l HeightFieldShape produces no result and emits a
warning.
//! [query_shape]

//! [unordered_hits_note]
\note Hits are returned in spatial tree traversal order, not sorted by distance. Sort the
list yourself if you need depth order.
//! [unordered_hits_note]

//! [mtd_overlap_note]
\note If \a shape already overlaps a body at its starting position, that hit reports a
negative \c distance whose magnitude is the penetration depth, along with the \c position
and \c normal needed to separate the two shapes.
//! [mtd_overlap_note]
